:: StoryTitle
Math Kingdom: The Number Gate

:: StoryData
{"ifid":"B62B6810-4D10-4AF2-A815-AF74B70A1255","format":"Harlowe","format-version":"3.3.9","start":"Arrival"}

:: Arrival
The Number Storm has sealed the gates of Math Kingdom. You are the Courier, carrying a map of the broken paths.

A voice calls from the gatehouse. What do you do?

[[Speak to the Gatekeeper->Gatekeeper]]
[[Inspect the sealed gate->Gate]]

:: Gatekeeper
"Three numbers lie beyond the platforms," says the Gatekeeper. "Their sum must be exactly ten. Reach the green portal before the sands run out."

[[Ask about the storm->Storm]]
[[Accept the challenge->Ready]]

:: Gate
An inscription glows: 2 + 3 + 5 = ?

[[Answer ten->Ready]]
[[Search for clues->Gatekeeper]]

:: Storm
"The storm feeds on doubt," the Gatekeeper explains. "Plan your jumps, watch the clock, and trust your arithmetic."

[[Begin the journey->Ready]]

:: Ready
You step toward the first platform. Three golden numbers wait ahead, and the green gate flickers in the distance.

Your objective: collect 2, 3, and 5, then reach the exit with a sum of 10.

[[Enter Math Kingdom->Ending]]
[[Ask for the instructions again->Gatekeeper]]

:: Ending
The adventure begins! Return to the Unity game to play the platforming level.

[[Replay the introduction->Arrival]]
